requires 1.4.0
# Generated by app/ssf.py — do not hand-edit (regenerate via /stack/render).
# Runs as its own siril-cli process, one per night (Handoff.md gotcha #8:
# running multiple sequences' calibrate+register in one Siril session is
# a confirmed severe performance cliff, not just additive). No register
# here — that happens in a separate final step (register_stack_single.ssf.j2
# or register_stack_merge.ssf.j2) once every night's pp_light exists.
# NOTE: `cd "path"` strips quotes correctly, but `-key="path"` style
# options (-out=/-dark=/-flat=) do NOT — keep those unquoted.
cd "{{ raw_lights }}"
convert light -out={{ process_dir }}
cd "{{ process_dir }}"
calibrate light -dark={{ dark_master }} -flat={{ flat_master }}{{ cc_flag }}{{ osc_flags }}
close
